+{
+  "baguette-eternity-band:Amethyst": "Photo edit of a real photograph, not a new picture. Image 1 is a photograph of a customer. Image 2 is a studio photograph of one jewellery piece: gold band of amethyst baguettes. Place the piece from Image 2 on the customer in Image 1 as if it had been photographed on them in the same moment with the same camera, and ensure that the customer and everything else in Image 1 remain completely unchanged. Preserve the piece from Image 2 exactly: identical gold, rectangular purple amethyst baguettes set crosswise side by side all the way round, held by small gold claws, same shapes, same proportions, same lustre, same gold tone. Do not redesign, restyle, resize or add anything to the piece; they must stay rectangular baguettes in one row, never round stones and never a plain band. Take only the jewellery from Image 2, never its plaster block, background, surface or shadows. CRITICAL SCALE: the piece is 6.8 mm wide, about 40% of the finger's width; an adult ring finger is about 16 to 18 mm wide at its base; it must look small, light and real on the body, never costume-sized and never enlarged to be seen, with a soft believable contact shadow where it touches the skin. Placement: at the base of the ring finger, the fourth finger counting the thumb as the first; the band wraps the finger in perspective with no gap between band and skin, and the hand keeps exactly five fingers in the same pose. Keep the person and the photograph exactly as they are: the same face, features, expression, skin tone and skin texture with visible pores, hair, makeup, body, clothing, pose, background, framing, crop and colour; no retouching, no smoothing, no slimming, no skin lightening, no beautifying, and never change, remove or reveal any clothing. If a ring is already on that finger, replace it; leave other rings, bangles and mehndi exactly as they are. Light the piece only with the light already in Image 1, from the same direction and in the same colour, with one small crisp specular highlight on the gold and a single catchlight in each stone, so it reads as real metal, never plastic. If Image 1 does not clearly show a hand with its fingers, do not create an image and reply only with the word NO_HAND. Return one photograph with the same aspect ratio and framing as Image 1, with no text, no logo, no watermark, no border, no second view and no other jewellery added.",
