+  "bold-nocturne-chain:default": "Photo edit of a real photograph, not a new picture. Image 1 is a photograph of a customer. Image 2 is a studio photograph of one jewellery piece: chunky gold oval link chain. Place the piece from Image 2 on the customer in Image 1 as if it had been photographed on them in the same moment with the same camera, and ensure that the customer and everything else in Image 1 remain completely unchanged. Preserve the piece from Image 2 exactly: identical gold, polished oval links with exactly 1 link set in clear pavé, same shapes, same proportions, same lustre, same gold tone. Do not redesign, restyle, resize or add anything to the piece; every other link stays plain polished gold, never pavé. Take only the jewellery from Image 2, never its plaster block, background, surface or shadows. CRITICAL SCALE: the piece is 46 cm long with links about 10 to 12 mm wide, each link about one iris width; at 46 cm it rests on the collarbones; the coloured iris of the eye is about 11.7 mm across; it must look small, light and real on the body, never costume-sized and never enlarged to be seen, with a soft believable contact shadow where it touches the skin. Placement: resting on the collarbones, the pavé link at front centre; the chain follows the curve of the neck and collarbones and lies on the skin or over the clothing as a real chain would, the back of the chain hidden behind the neck, and hair in front stays in front. Keep the person and the photograph exactly as they are: the same face, features, expression, skin tone and skin texture with visible pores, hair, makeup, body, clothing, pose, background, framing, crop and colour; no retouching, no smoothing, no slimming, no skin lightening, no beautifying, and never change, remove or reveal any clothing. If a necklace is already worn, replace it with this piece and leave everything else exactly as it is. Light the piece only with the light already in Image 1, from the same direction and in the same colour, with one small crisp specular highlight on the gold and a single catchlight in each stone, so it reads as real metal, never plastic. If Image 1 does not clearly show the neck and both shoulders, do not create an image and reply only with the word NO_NECK. Return one photograph with the same aspect ratio and framing as Image 1, with no text, no logo, no watermark, no border, no second view and no other jewellery added.",
